# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dockerignore applies to the whole BUILD CONTEXT, not per-stage. Both stages
# below share it, so it cannot simply exclude everything the nginx stage must
# not serve — the `fetcher` stage needs scripts/ and requirements.txt, and
# excluding them here made `docker-compose run fetcher` fail at COPY.
#
# So: keep the context minimal, keep scripts/ and requirements*.txt IN it, and
# let the frontend stage copy an explicit file list rather than `COPY .`.
# That is what actually keeps .git/ and friends out of the public web root
# (without it, /.git/config was reachable — full source and secret disclosure
# on a public fork).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
tests
bootstrap.ps1

# Bulky or private data — never needed by either stage.
data/archive
data/.cache
data/*.jsonl
data/.alert_state.json
data/.digest_state.json
data/.feed_meta.json

**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.env
.venv
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
